  "def-nagata-scheme-theoretic-closure",
  "def-nagata-scheme-theoretic-image",
  "def-nagata-two-open-boundary-loci",
  "def-nagata-two-open-comparison-space",
  "def-nagata-two-open-graph-extensions",
  "def-nagata-two-open-intermediate-schemes"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "The two generic maps have the same image in $U$, so their pair lands in\n$V_1\\times_UV_2=V_{12}$. Composing with the canonical image-factor map\ngives a factorization of the generic pair through $X_{12}$. The map\n$A\\to K$ is injective because a valuation ring is a domain. Apply\n[lemma-nagata-valuation-factor-closed] to the closed immersion\n$X_{12}\\hookrightarrow X_1\\times_SX_2$ and the morphism\n$(g_1,g_2)\\colon\\operatorname{Spec}(A)\\to X_1\\times_SX_2$. It extends the\ngeneric factorization to all of $\\operatorname{Spec}(A)$.",
   "uses": [
    "lemma-nagata-valuation-factor-closed"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
 "proof_deps": [
